  "rationale": {
    "component-prop-types": "Every prop type / variant enum / options type for a popup/components/* or hooks/* file is a library API surface: exported so TypeScript consumers (including future Storybook stories and tests) can type props without re-declaring them. Removing forces consumers to re-derive via `React.ComponentProps<typeof X>`, which is brittle. Do not delete these unless the component itself is deleted.",
    "test-helpers": "Functions named `*ForTests` or `__*ForTests` are test-only internals that may be referenced by tests via `vi.mock()` indirection or by integration harnesses whose call graph ts-unused-exports cannot resolve. Keep these exports to preserve the test contract.",
    "barrel-reexports": "`micro/index.ts`, `background/stages/index.ts` and similar barrel files are curated public module interfaces that re-export symbols for selective import. Tree-shaking makes unused re-exports zero-cost at runtime, and having the barrel lets consumers import `from '.../micro'` instead of reaching into deep internal paths.",
    "release-mode-flags": "`IS_DEVELOPMENT_BUILD`, `IS_NON_PRODUCTION_BUILD` in `popup/lib/release-mode.ts` are referenced only via `vi.mock('.../release-mode', { ... })` in tests. The mock key is a string literal that ts-unused-exports cannot trace to an import statement.",
    "telemetry-plumbing": "Cold-start timing (`ColdStartTimings`, `recordColdStart`, etc.) and SLO plumbing (`HandlerSlo`, `SloSnapshot`, etc.) are emitted by the runtime but consumed downstream by observability collectors that link at package boundaries ts-unused-exports does not trace.",
    "motion-design-tokens": "`popup/design/motion.ts` exports the full motion design system (spring names, easings, durations, keyframes). Individual tokens may not all be referenced in the initial UI, but the file IS the documented design-system interface.",
    "vite-config-default": "`vite.config.ts` `export default` is consumed by Vite itself via ESM import at build time, outside the TypeScript module graph that ts-unused-exports walks.",
    "package-public-api": "Package barrel files like `packages/*/src/index.ts` are the public API surface of each package. Exports there are intentionally available to external consumers (SDK users, future workspaces, audit tools) even when not yet imported by the extension. Removing them would silently break downstream forks and the extracted-SDK roadmap documented in each package's README."
  }
}
